{%- if lcp -%}
<a class="u-url sr-only" href="{{ page.url }}">{{ title }}</a>{% comment %} Visual fix: sr-only so the permalink's own title isn't printed twice (h1 above already carries p-name) — see types/article.liquid's comment. {% endcomment %}
{%- if date %}<time class="dt-published" datetime="{{ date | isoInstant }}">{{ date | humanDate }}</time>{% endif %}
{%- comment %} Task (visual fix): the image loop used to sit as a sibling
*before* `.content-grid`, so it inherited no width constraint beyond the
bare `img{max-width:100%}` reset — 100% of `.content-main`, which at
tmpl-page desktop widths is unbounded (sass/_layout.scss's own
`.tmpl-page .content-main{max-width:none}`), not the reading-measure column.
Moving the loop inside `.content-grid` (Task S3, already ported) gives it
the same already-ported width clamp every other in-content image gets — no
new CSS, just putting the image where the existing grid can reach it.
{% endcomment -%}
<div class="content-grid e-content">
{%- comment %} A photo post's `photo` is an array, so a post with more than one
   image is the carousel case. Wrapped the way the source wraps its own carousel
   (eleventy.config.js's `slides` shortcode): <is-land> defers the component
   until idle/visible, and <template data-island> means the module is only
   fetched if the island activates. Without JS the images are plain <img>
   elements in document order — <carou-scroll> is an unknown element and
   renders its children as-is. A single-photo post gets no carousel.
   {% endcomment -%}
{%- assign isCarousel = photo.size > 1 -%}
{%- if isCarousel %}<is-land on:idle on:visible>
{%- if JS_ENABLED %}<template data-island><script type="module" src="/carouscroll.js"></script></template>{% endif %}
<carou-scroll tabindex="0" class="carouscroll">{% endif %}
{%- for image in photo %}
{%- comment %} Task 18 (§7.4): the port source marks exactly one LCP image
   per page loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" (its own site avatar,
   default.liquid:16 in the source — this theme has no equivalent avatar).
   This partial's own image IS that page's LCP image, but only when
   rendered as the whole point of the page (entry.liquid, which sets
   `lcp`) — not when the same partial repeats down the homepage's h-feed
   (post-list-entry.liquid, which does not set it), where marking every
   listed photo eager would fight the real LCP image for priority instead
   of being one. Only the first image of a multi-photo post counts. {% endcomment -%}
{%- if forloop.first %}
<img class="u-photo" src="{{ image.url }}" alt="{{ image.alt | default: '' }}" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" eleventy:optional="keep">
{%- else %}
<img class="u-photo" src="{{ image.url }}" alt="{{ image.alt | default: '' }}" loading="lazy" decoding="async" eleventy:optional="keep">
{%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- if isCarousel %}</carou-scroll></is-land>{% endif %}
{%- comment %} Task 18 (§7.4): see types/article.liquid for why h2,h3. {% endcomment -%}
<heading-anchors selector="h2,h3">{{ content }}</heading-anchors>
</div>
{%- else -%}
{%- comment %} Task (visual fix, corrected from the prior S4 pass): a photo
is titleless by IndieWeb design (see types/note.liquid for the fallback
label / visible-link-text reasoning), but its "substance" isn't a sentence —
it's the photo. The visible link text is the image's own alt text (falling
back to a plain, non-date-duplicating "Photo" label only when the fixture
supplies none), matching `.posts-link` like every other type; the thumbnail
itself still sits in a second, plain (unmarked) link so u-url/p-name resolve
unambiguously to the one `u-*`-classed anchor. `.posts .spark-img` (already
ported, sass/theme-posts.scss) is the only rule in this port that constrains
an image's width *inside* `.posts` — reused here so the thumbnail reads as a
small preview next to the title instead of a near-full-width image blowing
out the row. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign firstPhoto = photo | first -%}
<a class="posts-link u-url" href="{{ page.url }}">{{ firstPhoto.alt | default: "Photo" }}</a>
{%- if firstPhoto %}
<a class="posts-thumb" href="{{ page.url }}"><img class="u-photo" src="{{ firstPhoto.url }}" alt="{{ firstPhoto.alt | default: '' }}" loading="lazy" decoding="async" eleventy:optional="keep"></a>
{%- endif %}
{{ socialHtml }}
{%- if date %}<time class="date dt-published" datetime="{{ date | isoInstant }}">{{ date | listingDate }}</time>{% endif %}
{%- endif -%}
